	Okay, first of all, if you don't have a whole lot of memory, forget
about running TW2!  I have around 4 megs of free RAM at all times on my 
system, so I didn't put too much thought into memory conservation for this 
game.  No, you're not going to need 4 megs to run this monster, but I WOULD
recommend at least a meg and a half free before a user enters the pfile.
TradeWars will do a memory check when the program first loads, and if there
is less than 900,000 bytes, if will drop the user back to the pfiles prompt.
However, that is the absolute minimum!  A user doing some vigorous game
playing will more than likely eat up a good meg to meg and a half of RAM!


SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
------------------

	If you happen to be running another version of TradeWars (1.05d or one
of the 2.0 Beta versions), CD to pfiles: and type "delete tradewars all", then
"delete TradeWars!" and "delete twmain".  Old TradeWars files are not
compatible with v2.0, and must be deleted.
	If you haven't already done so, un-lzh the "TradeWars2.0.lzh" archive
into a temporary directory somewhere, and type "execute tradewars.execute".
All necessary directories will be made, and all archives will be copied and
un-lzh'ed into their appropriate places.  NOTE:  Make sure you have the LZ
utility in your C: directory!!  If you still use Lharc, temporarily rename it
to LZ, or change the execute file accordingly!
	Alright, now you will need to add a couple of lines to your BBSEVENT0
file.  They are:

ALL	000	ALL	000	-o	RUNA	pfiles:TwNightlyMaint
ALL	000	ALL	000	-o	RUNA	pfiles:TwMaint

	You absolutely *MUST* run "TwNightlyMaint" each and every night at
midnight!  The game will get seriously FRIED if you don't!  If a player is
in the game when TwNightlyMaint is ran, it will automatically wait until they
quit the game before it begins.
	Why are there two TradeWars Maintenance programs?  TwNightlyMaint
updates all player files, moves the Borg and Q, moves and replenishes the
Klingons and Romulans, and much more.  No players are allowed to enter the
game while it is running.  TwMaint, however, simply scans all of the universe
sectors and makes the file for the "Game Statistics" command.  While it is
recommended that it be ran after TwNightlyMaint, it can be ran anytime, and
a player can be active in the game while it is running.


